  <prompt>Worktree C:\wt086, branch chore/remove-dead-shared-code (already created off origin/master; the main session has already committed the ADR-012 example removal and its CHANGELOG entry there). Land C-19 and resolve C-21, C-14, C-20, C-26, C-6, C-27 and the C-19 residual.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer. Cleanup is convergence and deletion with evidence, never a behaviour change in disguise.</role>
  <goal>Every item is either deleted with zero consumers proven, or kept with its documentation corrected; nothing that reads as live is dead.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>C-19: the CommandRegistry cluster (registry, EntityConfigurationService, CustomCommandFactory, Toolbar/CommandToolbar) is dead infra from a deleted PCF and carried a loop-over-selection deleteRecord. Task 080 deleted it on the ontology branch (commit 1c56cd29b). It KEPT useKeyboardShortcuts.ts because PageChrome/CommandBar.tsx imports it, but CommandBar itself appeared to have no consumers (#1113). C-21: OWNER DECISION 2026-10-03 is DELETE the Pillar-9 getAgentVisibleState client derivation (pillar9-visibility.ts and getWorkspaceWidgetVisibleStateFn). The server re-derives the shape itself and trims it to identity fields; wiring the client copy live would feed browser-computed data into an LLM prompt (#1112). C-14, C-20, C-26, C-6, C-27 are listed in the reuse audit table.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-080-six-hazards-deviations.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this work lands in its OWN pull request, not in the ontology PR #1111. Owner decision 2026-10-03: cleanup unrelated to ontology is fixed now (never deferred to an issue) but kept off the ontology branch so that PR stays reviewable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: work ONLY in the worktree named in the prompt. Do NOT edit anything in the ontology worktree C:\code_files\spaarke-wt-spaarke-ontology-platform-r1, including its TASK-INDEX.md and this POML. The main session records completion.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: run the affected package tests BEFORE applying any change (that run is the master baseline) and AFTER. Report both. A failure is pre-existing only if it appears in the baseline run; never assert pre-existing without that evidence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: install dependencies with npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund (root CLAUDE.md section 12). Discard every package-lock.json diff that npm install produces; lockfile churn is never part of this PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: never use --no-verify. If a pre-commit hook fails, fix the cause (usually a missing node_modules).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: you CANNOT write .claude/ paths. If one is needed, stop and report the exact text for the main session.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: when applying C-19 from the commit, EXCLUDE the StatusBadge hunk of src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/index.ts; StatusBadge is ontology work that stays on the ontology branch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: C-21 is DELETE, decided by the owner 2026-10-03. Trace every consumer of SerializedWidgetState.ts and WorkspaceTab.ts first and delete only the shim; keep any type with a live consumer. Do not change the server's C# re-derivation, which is the authoritative path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: C-26 deletes PcfDataverseClient, useDocumentMultiSelect and DraftSummaryFollowOnStep but KEEPS cancelHandoff, which is self-documented as intentional.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: C-27 is a RECORD only. Do NOT delete the output_pane widget components; they are lazily reachable. Record in the architecture doc that lists them that 6 of 7, plus redline-viewer and matters-dashboard, have no server producer.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Cleanup with evidence</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/reuse-verification-2026-10-02.md</file>
