  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above.</step>
    <step order="1">In the worktree named in the prompt, install root and affected-package dependencies, then run the affected package tests and record the result as the master baseline.</step>
    <step order="2">Apply the C-19 changes already written and verified on the ontology branch: git diff 1c56cd29b~1 1c56cd29b -- &lt;paths below&gt; | git apply. The commit is in the shared object store, so it is reachable from this worktree. Paths: src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/jest.config.js src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Toolbar/ src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/ src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/index.ts src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/index.ts (Toolbar hunk only).</step>
    <step order="3">C-19 residual (#1113): trace PageChrome/CommandBar.tsx reachability across src/solutions and src/client/pcf, including lazy and dynamic imports. If unreachable, delete it and useKeyboardShortcuts.ts; if reachable, keep both and say where they are used.</step>
    <step order="4">C-21: delete the Pillar-9 client shim per the owner decision, after tracing SerializedWidgetState.ts and WorkspaceTab.ts consumers.</step>
    <step order="5">C-14, C-20, C-26, C-6: for each, prove zero consumers by grep (including lazy imports) and delete; where an item has a live consumer, keep it and correct the misleading docstring or header instead.</step>
    <step order="6">C-27: record the producer gap in the architecture doc; delete nothing.</step>
    <step order="7">Put 'Closes #1112' and 'Closes #1113' in the PR body.</step>
    <step order="8">Run the affected package tests and builds again and compare against the baseline. Quote both outputs.</step>
    <step order="9">Commit with a conventional-commit message ending in the line: Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;. Push the branch and open a pull request against master, ready for review (not draft). The PR body states the item ids, says the work comes from the spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 reuse audit, and ends with: 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)</step>
    <step order="10">Report back: the PR URL, each acceptance criterion with evidence, files changed, the baseline and after test output, and any escalation.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a delete-or-adopt item (C-14 AI.Context hooks / ChatApiClient / chat-history trio, C-20 wizardRegistry, C-6 LegalWorkspaceRenderer) has a live consumer AND adopting it would change behaviour, STOP on that item and report it to the main session for an owner decision. Do not file it as an issue, and complete the others.</trigger>
  </escalation>

