  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A repo-wide grep finds no CommandRegistry, EntityConfigurationService, CustomCommandFactory or CommandToolbar outside git history and comments explaining the deletion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Pillar-9 client shim is deleted and every type that had a live consumer still compiles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each of C-14, C-20, C-26, C-6 is either deleted with zero consumers shown, or kept with its documentation corrected and the consumer cited.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: cancelHandoff and the output_pane widget components still exist.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR closes #1112 and #1113.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A pull request against master is open, ready for review, with the item ids in its body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the PR contains no package-lock.json changes and no file outside this task's scope.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The after-change test run has no failure that is absent from the master baseline run.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <completion date="2026-10-03">PR #1120 (056254e55, 16926ecf4, 8082b03d5, b443e4779); closes #1112 and #1113. Deleted: C-19 cluster plus CommandExecutor (main session verified its only other reference on master is the barrel this PR edits), PageChrome/CommandBar and useKeyboardShortcuts, the C-21 Pillar-9 shim (owner decision), C-14, C-20, C-26 (cancelHandoff kept), C-6. C-27 recorded only. Follow-ups: stale C# doc comments corrected (main session verified comment-only, so no publish-size delta), unused @spaarke/auth removed from AI.Context. ADR-012 table updated by the main session. Found a test already red on master (register-workspace-widgets, since 0e5d0fafd), routed to task 054. ChatSessionCard formatter judged most correct; routed to task 081. Open for reviewer: ADR-020 SemVer path-A exception for removing exports from private file-linked packages.</completion>
